{"paper": "SSC-CPO-Tier1-03-Oct-2023-Shift3.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 50, "tagged_count": 50, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "P", "added": false}, {"text": "S", "added": false}, {"text": "R", "added": false}, {"text": "Q", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "A shopkeeper allows a discount of 15% on an article and still makes a profit of 20%. What does the shopkeeper pay for an article whose marked price is ₹7,200?", "options": [{"text": "₹6,120", "added": false}, {"text": "₹5,120", "added": false}, {"text": "₹6,100", "added": false}, {"text": "₹5,100", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "What is the compound interest on a sum of ₹25,000 after three years at a rate of 12 percent per annum interest compounded yearly?", "options": [{"text": "₹9,824.00", "added": false}, {"text": "₹10,520.00", "added": false}, {"text": "₹9,956.86", "added": false}, {"text": "₹10,123.20", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "ci-formula", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "The least number which should be added to 1351 so that the sum is exactly divisible by 2,4,6 and 8 is:", "options": [{"text": "11", "added": false}, {"text": "15", "added": false}, {"text": "13", "added": false}, {"text": "17", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "divisibility-rules", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "In a ∆PQR and ∆ ABC, ∠ P = ∠A and AC = PR. Which of the following conditions is true for triangle PQR and ABC to be congruent?", "options": [{"text": "AB = PQ by SSS", "added": false}, {"text": "AB = PQ by SAS", "added": false}, {"text": "BC = QR by ASS", "added": false}, {"text": "∠Q = ∠B by AAA", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "congruence-and-similarity", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "12,500", "added": false}, {"text": "12,000", "added": false}, {"text": "13,500", "added": false}, {"text": "13,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "pie-chart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "A vendor bought a book marked at ₹850 at successive discounts of 20% and 10%, respectively. He spent ₹55 on transport and sold the book for ₹980. What will be his profit percentage (rounded off to 2 decimal places)?", "options": [{"text": "45.65%", "added": false}, {"text": "48.25%", "added": false}, {"text": "50.65%", "added": false}, {"text": "46.93%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "successive-discounts", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "Two numbers are in the ratio of 4 : 3. The product of their HCF and LCM is 2700. The difference between the numbers is:", "options": [{"text": "15", "added": false}, {"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "25", "added": false}, {"text": "105", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "Ramesh borrowed some money at rate of 5% per annum for the first four years, 8% per annum for the next six years, and 12% per annum for the period beyond ten years. If the total interest paid by him at the end of twelve years is ₹9,016, then find the money borrowed by Ramesh.", "options": [{"text": "₹9,816", "added": false}, {"text": "₹9,800", "added": false}, {"text": "₹9,016", "added": false}, {"text": "₹9,616", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "College D", "added": false}, {"text": "College C", "added": false}, {"text": "College B", "added": false}, {"text": "College A", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "The average weight of 15 people increases by 3.2 kg when a new person comes in place of one of them weighing 52 kg. The weight of the new person is:", "options": [{"text": "48 kg", "added": false}, {"text": "96 kg", "added": false}, {"text": "100 kg", "added": false}, {"text": "52 kg", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "Study the given graph and answer the following question. Number of boys and girls students in each section. The number of boy students in section B is approximately what percentage of the number of girl students in section E?", "options": [{"text": "25%", "added": false}, {"text": "55%", "added": false}, {"text": "45%", "added": false}, {"text": "15%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "mixed-graphs", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "expression-values", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "The length and the breadth of the floor of a rectangular hall are 126 feet and 90 feet, respectively. What will be the area (in square feet) of each of the largest identical square tiles that can be used to tile this floor in a way that no part of the floor remains uncovered?", "options": [{"text": "484", "added": false}, {"text": "256", "added": false}, {"text": "324", "added": false}, {"text": "196", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "Study the given table and answer the question that follows. The table shows the consumption of food grains per day (in grams) in the given set of following years. For which food grain consumption was there successive increase over the given set of years?", "options": [{"text": "Rice", "added": false}, {"text": "Pulses", "added": false}, {"text": "Coarse grains", "added": false}, {"text": "Wheat", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "The LCM of two prime numbers x and y (x > y) is 533. The value of 4y - x is:", "options": [{"text": "18", "added": false}, {"text": "11", "added": false}, {"text": "23", "added": false}, {"text": "21", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "complementary-angles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "38 days", "added": false}, {"text": "41 days", "added": false}, {"text": "37 days", "added": false}, {"text": "39 days", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "efficiency", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "Study the given table and answer the question that follows. The table shows the number of employees in five different organisations A, B, C, D and E in different departments. Which organisation has minimum number of employees?", "options": [{"text": "C", "added": false}, {"text": "B", "added": false}, {"text": "D", "added": false}, {"text": "E", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "If (48 ÷ 72 × 3) – [15 ÷ 8 × (40 – 32) – 10] + 2P = 6 ÷ 2, then find the value of P?", "options": [{"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "Mayur sold a watch at a profit of 7%. If he had sold it for ₹1,329 more, he would have gained 57%. Find the cost price (in ₹) of the watch.", "options": [{"text": "2580", "added": false}, {"text": "2658", "added": false}, {"text": "2420", "added": false}, {"text": "2856", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 26, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 27, "text": "Find the area of a rhombus if the perimeter of the rhombus is 52 cm, and one of its diagonals is 10 cm long.", "options": [{"text": "120 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "164 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "160 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "144 cm2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 28, "text": "The speed of a boat in still water is 20 km/h, while the river is flowing at a speed of 8 km/h and the time taken to cover a certain distance upstream is 6 h more than the time taken to cover the same distance downstream. Find the distance.", "options": [{"text": "120 km", "added": false}, {"text": "336 km", "added": false}, {"text": "126 km", "added": false}, {"text": "125 km", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Boats-Streams", "sub": "still-water-and-stream-speed", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 29, "text": "In an election between P and Q, P gets 40% of the total votes and thus loses by 10 votes. The total number of votes is:", "options": [{"text": "80", "added": false}, {"text": "50", "added": false}, {"text": "90", "added": false}, {"text": "70", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 30, "text": "The price of a treadmill is marked at ₹1,250. A shopkeeper earns a profit of 14% after allowing a discount of 14% on the marked price. Find the cost price (to the nearest rupee) of the treadmill.", "options": [{"text": "₹845", "added": false}, {"text": "₹840", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,043", "added": false}, {"text": "₹943", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "mp-sp-relation", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 31, "text": "Jeevan can do a piece of work alone in 42 days, while Rishi and Jeevan together can do the same piece of work in 27 days. How many days will Rishi take to complete the same piece of work alone?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 32, "text": "A person covers 28 km while walking at a speed of 8 km/h. How much distance (in km) will he cover in same time if he walks at a speed of 6 km/h?", "options": [{"text": "36", "added": false}, {"text": "28", "added": false}, {"text": "32", "added": false}, {"text": "21", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "basic-tsd", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 33, "text": "The area of an equilateral triangle is 173.2 cm2. Its side will be __________.", "options": [{"text": "20 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "22 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "17.32 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "21.32 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 34, "text": "In two circles centred at O and O’, the distance between the centres of both circles is 17 cm. The points of contact of a direct common tangent between the circles are P and Q. If the radii of both circles are 7 cm and 15 cm, respectively, then the length of PQ is equal to:", "options": [{"text": "15 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "17 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "10 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "22 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 35, "text": "If 4 men or 6 boys can finish a piece of work in 20 days, then in how many days can 6 men and 11 boys finish the same work?", "options": [{"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "7", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 36, "text": "Aditya sold article X at a profit of 23% and article Y at a loss of 13%. He earned a profit of ₹180 in the entire transaction. If article X costs ₹90 less than article Y, then what is the price of article Y (in ₹)?", "options": [{"text": "2,100", "added": false}, {"text": "2,007", "added": false}, {"text": "2,020", "added": false}, {"text": "2,050", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 37, "text": "If sin 2A = cos 15°, then the smallest positive value of A is:", "options": [{"text": "75°", "added": false}, {"text": "37.5°", "added": false}, {"text": "7.5°", "added": false}, {"text": "47.5°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "ratios-and-tables", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 38, "text": "In an election, Ajay and Mohan are contesting for the Secretary post in a trade union of 9000 workers. 80% of the workers cast their votes, out of which 20% votes were found invalid. Ajay defeated Mohan by 1152 votes. How many votes did Ajay get?", "options": [{"text": "3456", "added": false}, {"text": "2304", "added": false}, {"text": "4480", "added": false}, {"text": "3546", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 39, "text": "Find the third proportional to 16 and 20.", "options": [{"text": "25", "added": false}, {"text": "23", "added": false}, {"text": "24", "added": false}, {"text": "26", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 40, "text": "The area of a sector of a circle of radius 8 cm, formed by an arc of length 4.6 cm, is ____.", "options": [{"text": "6.3 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "9.2 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "18.4 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "12.6 cm2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "circle-sector-ring", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 41, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "Geometry", "added": false}, {"text": "Notebook", "added": false}, {"text": "Charts", "added": false}, {"text": "Pages", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "bar-graph", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 42, "text": "A solid sphere made of wax of radius 12 cm is melted and cast into solid hemispheres of radius 4 cm each. Find the number of such solid hemispheres.", "options": [{"text": "54", "added": false}, {"text": "27", "added": false}, {"text": "14", "added": false}, {"text": "28", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 43, "text": "The curved surface area (CSA) and the total surface area (TSA) of a hemisphere whose radius is 7 cm are:", "options": [{"text": "CSA – 350 cm2; TSA – 500 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "CSA – 320 cm2; TSA – 480 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "CSA – 412 cm2; TSA – 544 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "CSA – 308 cm2; TSA – 462 cm2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 44, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "1,500", "added": false}, {"text": "2,000", "added": false}, {"text": "1,440", "added": false}, {"text": "2,550", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "pie-chart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 45, "text": "If the radius of a sphere is doubled, then its surface area will be increased by:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 46, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "34 : 51", "added": false}, {"text": "38 : 55", "added": false}, {"text": "51 : 34", "added": false}, {"text": "55 : 38", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 47, "text": "Find the third proportional to 23 and 31.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 48, "text": "A speedboat, whose speed in 20 km/h in still water, goes 35 km downstream and comes back in a total of 8 hours. What is the speed of the stream?", "options": [{"text": "20 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "10 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "15 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "5 km/h", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Boats-Streams", "sub": "still-water-and-stream-speed", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 49, "text": "What is the HCF of 12, 18 and 42?", "options": [{"text": "123", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "60", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 50, "text": "If 60 litres of a milk solution has 40% milk in it, then how much milk should be added to make the milk 60% in the solution?", "options": [{"text": "30 litres", "added": false}, {"text": "25 litres", "added": false}, {"text": "20 litres", "added": false}, {"text": "35 litres", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}]}